# Fastify v4 vulnerabilities — all fixed in v5.
# Risk accepted: Key Vault has INGRESS_TRAFFIC_INTERNAL_ONLY so is not reachable
# from untrusted clients. Migrate to fastify v5 to resolve permanently.
CVE-2026-25223
GHSA-jx2c-rxcm-jvmq
GHSA-mrq3-vjjr-p77c
GHSA-444r-cwp2-x5xf

# picomatch ReDoS in npm's own bundled copy (usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/).
# Not in our app code — cannot be fixed via npm overrides.
# Fixed in picomatch 4.0.4/3.0.2/2.3.2 but updating system npm is outside scope.
CVE-2026-33671

# sigstore certificateOIDs verification bypass in npm's own bundled copy
# (usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/ — npm vendors sigstore for install provenance).
# Not an app dependency (absent from package-lock); cannot be fixed via npm overrides.
# npm's provenance verifier is never invoked at runtime, and the Key Vault is
# INGRESS_TRAFFIC_INTERNAL_ONLY. Fixed in sigstore 4.1.1 (ships with a newer system npm).
CVE-2026-48815

# node-tar DoS (gzip bomb / malformed header) in npm's own bundled copy
# (usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/ — npm vendors tar for its own package
# extraction). Absent from our package-lock entirely -- not an app dependency,
# cannot be fixed via npm overrides. npm is never invoked at runtime (the
# container's CMD is `node dist/main.js`), and the Key Vault is
# INGRESS_TRAFFIC_INTERNAL_ONLY. Fixed in tar 7.5.18/7.5.19 (ships with a
# newer system npm).
CVE-2026-59873
CVE-2026-59874

# brace-expansion ReDoS in npm's own bundled copy (usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/
# -- npm vendors its own minimatch/brace-expansion for internal glob matching).
# brace-expansion IS in our package-lock, but only via eslint -> minimatch, a
# devDependency; the image's dependencies stage runs `npm ci --only=production`,
# which excludes devDependencies, so that copy never reaches the final image.
# The version Trivy flags in the scanned image is npm's own internal copy, not
# reachable at runtime. Fixed in brace-expansion 5.0.7/2.1.2/1.1.16 (ships with
# a newer system npm).
CVE-2026-13149
